From f5bca64bf2f03c0bf2b5b31188ed979376574c74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Tojnar <jtojnar@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Aug 2024 02:57:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/25] Adjust flake8 rules
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hound enables flake8-black [out of the box](https://www.github.com/houndci/hound/issues/1769).
When we change certain files, it will whine that “Black would make changes”.
But if we run black locally, Hound will spit out flake8’s complaints about the changes black made.

As per the [black recommendations](https://black.readthedocs.io/en/stable/guides/using_black_with_other_tools.html#flake8),
we now exclude these three rules:

- E203: Whitespace before ':' (https://www.flake8rules.com/rules/E203.html)
- E501: Line too long (82 > 79 characters) (https://www.flake8rules.com/rules/E501.html)
- E701: Multiple statements on one line (colon) (https://www.flake8rules.com/rules/E701.html)

and add a flake8-bugbear which is already enabled on hound (https://www.github.com/houndci/hound/issues/1707).
Specifically, we enable the following rule:

- B950: Line too long https://github.com/PyCQA/flake8-bugbear#:~:text=b950%3A%20line%20too%20long%2E

(cherry picked from commit 3cade4759c28f4c8ac934acec74e512fab7e3fbf)
---
 setup.cfg | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index 49965f1f4..2ccc25a70 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -20,7 +20,9 @@ verbosity=2
 # Syntax checking:
 
 [flake8]
-ignore = E266,W503,E251,E226,BLK100
+max-line-length = 80
+extend-select = B950
+ignore = E203,E266,E501,E701,W503,E251,E226,BLK100
 exclude =
     .git,
     __pycache__,

